      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $s=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\right)$ and $c=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\right)$. The **double-angle formula** gives $\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{15}\\right)=2sc$.\n\n Also, $\\cot\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\right)=\\frac{c}{s}$.\n\nRewrite the quotient ratio and cancel. Use $s^2+c^2=1$, factor the difference of squares, then cancel the matching binomial.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2sc\\frac{c}{s}}{(1-s)} &=\\frac{2c^2}{(1-s)} \\\\ &=2\\frac{1-s^2}{(1-s)} \\\\ &=2\\frac{(1-s)(1+s)}{(1-s)} \\\\ &=2(1+s) \\\\ &=2\\left(1+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll cancellations use nonzero factors in the original expression.",
